.TH KIBAN 1 "2026-11-01" "kiban" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kiban \- run Docker and local dev databases at full speed on macOS and Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiban
.RI [ options ] " command" " " [ arguments ]
.br
.B kiban doctor
.br
.B kiban version
.br
.B kiban help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiban
starts Docker and the databases a project needs. On a Mac it runs a Colima VM
with Apple's Virtualization framework and virtiofs, sized from the machine. It
reads the hardware, so a terminal running under Rosetta still gets a native
aarch64 VM with Rosetta for x86_64 images. On Linux it drives the Docker engine
itself, with no VM.
.PP
Every service listens on 127.0.0.1 only and keeps its data in named volumes
plus a folder under the data directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR start " [" \fIprofile\fR ]
Start the VM on a Mac, or the Docker engine on Linux.
.TP
.BR stop " [" \fIprofile\fR ]
Stop it.
.TP
.BI up " service" ...
Create a service the first time, start it after that. The services are mongo,
postgres, redis, valkey, redict and ubuntu.
.TP
.BR down " [" \fIcontainer\fR ...]
Stop containers. With none named, pick from the running ones.
.TP
.BR shell " [" \fIcontainer\fR ]
Open a shell in a container, bash when it has one.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \fIcontainer\fR ]
Follow a container's log.
.TP
.B status
Show every service, its state, its address and its image.
.TP
.BI reset " service"
Delete a service's container, volumes and data folder, after the service name
is typed back.
.TP
.BR prune " [" \fIprofile\fR ]
Delete every container, image, volume and build cache, after the profile name
is typed back. Anything labelled keep survives.
.TP
.BR purge " [" \fIprofile\fR ]
Prune, then delete the VM and its disks on a Mac.
.TP
.B config
Show every setting, its value and where it came from.
.TP
.B doctor
List the tools kiban needs and whether each is installed. Exits non-zero only
when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and the platform.
.TP
.B help
Print the usage page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cpus " N" ", " \-\-memory " GIB" ", " \-\-disk " GIB"
VM size. The defaults scale with the machine: half its cores up to 4, half its
memory up to 8 GiB, a quarter of its disk up to 64 GiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " aarch64" | x86_64
VM architecture. Default the machine's.
.TP
.BI \-\-vm\-type " vz" | qemu | krunkit
VM type. Default vz.
.TP
.BR \-\-rosetta ", " \-\-no\-rosetta
Run x86_64 images through Rosetta. Default yes on Apple Silicon.
.TP
.BI \-\-mount\-type " virtiofs" | 9p | sshfs
How the home folder reaches the VM. Default virtiofs.
.TP
.BR \-\-mount\-inotify ", " \-\-no\-mount\-inotify
Pass file events into the VM. Default no.
.TP
.BI \-\-dns " list"
DNS servers for the VM, separated by commas. Default the host's.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " path"
Folder for service data. Default ~/Docker.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print status or config as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
Every option that takes a value also takes the form
.IR \-\-name = value ,
and
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every setting has a variable that sets its default:
.BR KIBAN_PROFILE ,
.BR KIBAN_CPUS ,
.BR KIBAN_MEMORY ,
.BR KIBAN_DISK ,
.BR KIBAN_ARCH ,
.BR KIBAN_VM_TYPE ,
.BR KIBAN_ROSETTA ,
.BR KIBAN_MOUNT_TYPE ,
.BR KIBAN_MOUNT_INOTIFY ,
.BR KIBAN_DNS ,
.BR KIBAN_DATA_DIR
and
.BR KIBAN_JSON ,
and per service
.BI KIBAN_ SERVICE _IMAGE
and
.BI KIBAN_ SERVICE _PORT ,
.BR KIBAN_MONGO_USER ,
.BR KIBAN_MONGO_PASSWORD ,
.BR KIBAN_POSTGRES_USER ,
.BR KIBAN_POSTGRES_PASSWORD ,
.B KIBAN_POSTGRES_SHM
and
.BI KIBAN_ SERVICE _MAXMEMORY
for redis, valkey and redict. An option on the command line wins.
.TP
.B KIBAN_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B KIBAN_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure or refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR colima (1),
.BR docker (1)
